# head(1)

## NAME

head - output the first part of files

## SYNOPSIS

    head [-n lines | -c bytes] [file...]

## DESCRIPTION

Writes the first 10 lines of each file (or standard input). With two or more files, each is preceded by `==> name <==`.

## OPTIONS

- `-n lines`: write this many lines (also `-lines`)
- `-c bytes`: write this many bytes

## EXIT STATUS

- `0`: success
- `1`: an error occurred for some operand
- `2`: usage error

## SEE ALSO

tail(1), cat(1)
